At the same time, several features support BBB entry. The neutral fraction is 0.9999, which is extremely high and suggests the molecule is overwhelmingly neutral at physiological pH; that strongly favors passive membrane diffusion. The alkyl chloride count is 2, adding nonpolar character that can help lipophilicity. The minimum absolute partial charge is 0.2532, indicating a modest charge distribution rather than a highly polar, strongly ionized profile, which is also somewhat favorable. The rotatable-bond count is 6, which is only moderately flexible and still within the range often seen for CNS-active compounds, so flexibility is not excessively high. The aliphatic carbocycle count is 0, so there is no added saturated carbocycle burden, although this also means the scaffold does not gain extra rigid hydrophobic character from that source.

Overall, the high TPSA, low logP/logD, and polar atom burden argue against BBB penetration, but the nearly complete neutral fraction, some hydrophobic halogen content, moderate flexibility, and modest partial-charge character provide enough compensating support that the molecule is more consistent with crossing the BBB than not crossing it."
